# Copy to .env.release.local and explicitly export in your shell; never commit secrets.
# Default packaging/releases use local ad-hoc signing; no Apple account or certificate is needed.
# Leave identity/team/notary/config overrides unset for this default.
# Optional Developer ID distribution: select your release account's certificate.
# Get its fingerprint and team ID from: security find-identity -v -p codesigning
# Optional notarization: save your release account's app-specific password interactively (never put it in this file):
# xcrun notarytool store-credentials 1git-notary --apple-id APPLE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL --team-id TEAM_ID
# Export the certificate and team to enable Developer ID signing:
# ONEGIT_MACOS_SIGNING_IDENTITY=YOUR_40_CHARACTER_CERTIFICATE_FINGERPRINT
# ONEGIT_MACOS_TEAM_ID=YOUR_10_CHARACTER_APPLE_TEAM_ID
# Leave this unset or empty to publish signed apps without notarization credentials.
# Set it to 1git-notary later to enable notarization, stapling and Gatekeeper checks.
# ONEGIT_MACOS_NOTARY_PROFILE=
# release:macos --dry-run skips Apple submission and never publishes.
# Do not combine Developer ID settings with the local pin override or ad-hoc mode.

# Optional self-signed builds: run bun run setup:signing:macos once, then opt in with
# ONEGIT_MACOS_SIGNING_CONFIG=apps/gpuix/native/macos-signing.json (use an absolute path).
# Its public pin is native/macos-signing.json; the private key remains in Keychain.
# Optional CI/test public pin override (does not import or replace any identity):
# ONEGIT_MACOS_SIGNING_CONFIG=/secure/config/macos-signing.json
# release:macos reads the bucket/account/feed URL from the saved Alchemy stack.
# By default release:macos reads the existing public key from Keychain account
# dev.1git.gpuix. It never creates or rotates a key. Optional explicit override:
# ONEGIT_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY=YOUR_BASE64_ED25519_PUBLIC_KEY

# Optional existing Alchemy profile; omitted uses personal. --profile overrides it.
# ALCHEMY_PROFILE=personal
# R2 reads reuse this profile; writes use the deployed native-R2 publisher
# and request signatures from the same existing Sparkle key used for updates.
# No temporary API tokens, token-provisioning permission, or S3 credentials.

# Optional secure CI file. Without this, signing reads account dev.1git.gpuix in Keychain.
# File-based signing requires ONEGIT_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY above; no Keychain fallback.
# ONEGIT_UPDATE_KEY_FILE=/secure/path/to/sparkle-private-key
